# Security

## Never commit / paste into this repo

Master passwords, Fine-Grained PATs, invite links (`#i=TANDEM2.…`), pairing codes, legacy cleartext invites, real plaintext vault JSON.

## Trust model

App origin is fully trusted while unlocked (XSS ⇒ game over). Harden; don’t pretend GitHub encryption fixes XSS.

## Crypto (`src/lib/crypto.ts`)

- PBKDF2 100k + AES-256-GCM; envelope `v: 1` (`salt`, `iv`, `ciphertext`)
- New IV every encrypt; keep state `salt` stable unless deliberately migrating
- Do not weaken iterations or log decrypted state / secrets

## Storage

- Password + vault cache: **sessionStorage** only (`clearSessionSecrets` on lock)
- PAT + GitHub config: localStorage (`tandem.github`)
- Invite QR embeds **PAT**, not password — treat as secret

## Data repo

Always private. PAT scoped Contents R/W to that repo only.

## Export

Settings JSON export is **plaintext** — never add sample real-household fixtures to the repo.
